@startuml auth-sequence-jwks
title Gym auth: how other services verify tokens

actor User
participant "PWA" as PWA
participant "Other service\nAPI Gateway" as OtherAPIGW
participant "API Gateway\nJWT Authorizer" as Authorizer
participant "Auth API Gateway" as AuthAPIGW
participant "JwksLambda" as JwksLambda

PWA -> OtherAPIGW : request with Bearer <access JWT>
OtherAPIGW -> Authorizer : validate token
Authorizer -> AuthAPIGW : GET /.well-known/jwks.json\n(cached 10m)
AuthAPIGW -> JwksLambda : invoke
JwksLambda --> AuthAPIGW : { keys: [EC/P-256 public key] }
AuthAPIGW --> Authorizer : JWKS doc
Authorizer -> Authorizer : verify ES256 sig, iss, aud, exp
Authorizer --> OtherAPIGW : allow
OtherAPIGW -> OtherAPIGW : route to target Lambda\nwith sub claim available

note right of Authorizer
Issuer, audience, and JWKS URL are
exported both as CDK stack outputs
and as public SSM parameters under
/gym/auth/public/*, so every other
service's CDK stack reads them with
StringParameter.valueFromLookup.
end note

@enduml
